From: GameShellNeo contributors
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: axp20x: mask the low byte of variable-width readings

The helper combines a high byte with width - 8 low bits, but currently
ORs in the entire low register. Unused bits can therefore contaminate the
high portion of a 9-15 bit reading. Mask them before combining the bytes.
For 16-bit callers the mask retains the whole low byte.

Keep the existing 9-16 bit caller contract, register order and error
propagation. This does not establish an atomic ADC snapshot or change
scaling, calibration or charger controls.

diff --git a/include/linux/mfd/axp20x.h b/include/linux/mfd/axp20x.h
--- a/include/linux/mfd/axp20x.h
+++ b/include/linux/mfd/axp20x.h
@@ -986,7 +986,7 @@
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
-	result |= reg_val;
+	result |= reg_val & (BIT(width - 8) - 1);
 
 	return result;
 }
